    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0444" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg340"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 270.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit to you herewith for your
                    information a translation of a note<anchor n="*" xml:id="d247-f1"/> from the
                    minister of Venezuela at this capital concerning the Venezuelan boundary
                    question.</p>
                <p>The statements of the Venezuelan minister are interesting from the historical
                    point of view, especially in regard to the shifting nature of the British
                    contention; but, as the essential elements of the determination of the problem
                    are matters of record, there should be no difficulty in reaching a just
                    conclusion on the merits, and, in the expectation of such a result, it is proper
                    to refrain from any prejudgment of opinion on the merits of the British
                    contention.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d247-f1" n="*" xml:id="d247-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see note of May 20, 1890, from the minister from Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
